    "title": "Stanley County Hosts Philip in First Home Doubleheader - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Jon Winkler ,\n3 hours ago For the first time this season the Stanley County Buffalo boys basketball team will be home as the Buffs host the Philip Scotties in a girls and boys doubleheader. The Lady Buffs will again look for its first win of the season as they face the Philip Lady Scotties to open up the night. The Lady Scotties are 1-1 after the 65-51 win on Tuesday night at home against Belle Fourche to even its record. Philip went 10-10 last year falling in the Region 7B playoffs. Philip beat Stanley County by 23 last year. Stanley County is at 0-4 with a near win over White River and the offense is still gaining momentum. Addy Deal’s 31 points on Tuesday led the Lady Buffs and as more continue to contribute the offense can gain traction. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
